{"id": "EUVD-2026-101874", "enisaUuid": "689b076a-da33-383e-b80c-aba23823745c", "description": "The IPv6 UDP send path for unconnected sockets did not apply the jail policy of rewriting a loopback destination address to the jail's primary IPv6 address.\n\nA process in a classic (non-VNET) jail can send UDP datagrams to services listening on the host's IPv6 loopback address, bypassing jail network isolation.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T06:58:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:36:07", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N", "references": ["https://security.freebsd.org/advisories/FreeBSD-SA-26:69.udp.asc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-101303"], "assigner": "freebsd", "epss": 0.36, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05f3569e-7120-3f08-b976-281897d3d807", "product": {"name": "FreeBSD", "vendor": {"name": "FreeBSD"}}, "product_version": "15.0-RELEASE <p14"}, {"id": "56a8da1c-afdb-3ff1-a861-15b800acfe54", "product": {"name": "FreeBSD", "vendor": {"name": "FreeBSD"}}, "product_version": "14.4-RELEASE <p10"}, {"id": "74bb3707-6125-3714-a970-6abd4ad34058", "product": {"name": "FreeBSD", "vendor": {"name": "FreeBSD"}}, "product_version": "15.1-RELEASE <p4"}, {"id": "a4970184-1f3d-3380-9863-7c93b65ba3ba", "product": {"name": "FreeBSD", "vendor": {"name": "FreeBSD"}}, "product_version": "14.5-RELEASE <p1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "347baa82-b58f-3dab-9a97-58fcf8b44bc2", "vendor": {"name": "FreeBSD"}}], "isExploited": false}